  "notes": [
    "The earlier 273-record source epoch is preserved in validation-domestic-iraq-273-pre-extra-aluminium.json with its historical source-bound packets.",
    "The current offline catalogue has 277 records; four additional Iraq-local aluminium manufacturers are source leads only and add no product or offer records.",
    "The 31,989 physical scopes are represented by 7,042 sourcing requirement groups in the federated packet; 137 were evaluated and 6,905 remain pending.",
    "Current source-bound packets use candidate-specific process snapshots, so unrelated sibling laminate study processes do not leak into one another’s publication inputs.",
    "The sourcing package hierarchy partitions 27,216 located occurrences into 191 draft inquiry scopes; 4,773 unlocated obligations remain separate, with 230 non-additive contextual links covering 4,766 of them.",
    "The current material takeoff records 4,780,578.4 kg of gross located stock mass and 1,804.81 m3 of nominal concrete stock geometry; installed mass and price remain unknown.",
    "Iraqi regional cost screens use published material statistics plus explicit labour-hour scenarios and a 20% uplift on direct material plus base labour; they are estimates, not supplier quotations or installed costs.",
    "The 2026 CSO price screen and the 2025 regional cost reference are separate dated evidence sets; both map concrete recipes to the same 81 stock groups but produce different scenario rates.",
    "The GFRP local-fabrication comparison includes 9 Baghdad and 135 regional labour scenarios for three 10 m2 study recipes. Material prices are UK catalogue extensions converted at a dated non-executable GBP/IQD reference; core/adhesive, tooling, consumables, import cost, QA and qualification remain open.",
    "Regional wage averages are construction-worker base wages used as labour proxies, not measured factory charge-out rates; the 20% uplift is unallocated and is not verified as overhead, profit, tax or contingency.",
    "Four new domestic aluminium leads (Asia Aluminum, Alko, Baxi Siwail and IIALCO) are unpriced and unqualified. The current Ur Company price observation remains the cost basis for existing aluminium profile/sheet scenarios.",
    "All sourcing packets remain research-only: no supplier communications were sent, no selected reference changed, no complete installed/whole-life cost is established, and no physical qualification is claimed."
  ],
